First thing to learn: news software isn't magic, it
takes real time to accomplish its work. On a busy
system, your article can take five to twenty minutes
to show up on that very system, from the time you
select "post message" or "send" or whatever is the
enabling mechanism in your news client software. On
Google Groups, that time, they say, can extend to
_nine_ _whole_ _hours_, and they are correct, it
often does. Don't do a prompt repost because "it
must not have worked"; not seeing it immediately is
_not_ a sign of trouble. So far your article has
shown up three times on the system I use.

xanthian.

As to "no white wizards", NetHack wizards would have
to forego using most of the existing spells to rate
as "lawful". Lawful Wizard probably isn't seen as a
role anyone would like to play under such
limitations.

Moreover, NetHack is _full_ of arbitrary
limitations. Being arbitrary doesn't make them
wrong. Keeping the game size within the limits of
quite old technology is a goal NetHack has met for
years, and that means it cannot be everything to all
users.  Nor can it perfectly mimic what the mind
insists is "logical" or "realistic". It is, after
all, a game, not a battle training simulator for
some armed forces customer.


